findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config tests and implementation use unwrap_or_default without distinguishing NotFound
    from parse/permission errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Dev implemented CWE-209 sanitization: ServerError(_) Display writes generic
    message, not the inner string. Reviewer verified this as V2. TEA also wrote CWE-209
    tests for error display.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote CWE-113 header injection tests for tenant ID. Dev implemented\
    \ with_tenant_validated that rejects CR/LF. However, SiemClient.tenant_id still\
    \ uses raw String internally rather than Option<TenantId> from axiathon-core,\
    \ so the finding is partially caught \u2014 injection is prevented but the type-safety\
    \ improvement of using TenantId is missed."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev added dependencies with direct version strings instead of workspace
    = true. No phase flagged this inconsistency with workspace dependency management.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding F9: ''No #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] on RawConfig.
    Typos like api_rul or timeot will be silently ignored, falling back to defaults.''
    This covers the same silent-ignore issue, though the specific token scenario was
    not called out.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in config tests. TEA wrote config tests but included this flawed assertion
    pattern.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    with 'let _ = config'. TEA wrote config tests but included this no-op test pattern.
